Passive Mix Bus: 

Tie the far ends of all four summing resistors (10 kΩ, 33 kΩ, 27 kΩ, 27 kΩ) together and run that node to the Tip of your 1/4" or 3.5 mm output jack (with Sleeve tied to System GND).

​Bonus Master Tone Knob: 

You can also wire one of those blue rotary pots mounted below your sliders as a passive low-pass tone control right at the output (Mix Bus \rightarrow rotary pot wiper/end lug \rightarrow 47 nF cap to GND) to roll off harsh digital harmonics on the fly.  